@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+# Name
+
+`nix-store --import-nar` - import one NAR at a known store path and bind its attestation sidecar
+
+# Synopsis
+
+`nix-store` `--import-nar` *store-path* *nar-file*
+  [`--nar-hash` *sri*]
+  [`--references` *store-path*]…
+  [`--deriver` *drv-path*]
+  [`--attestation-json` *file*]
+  [`--attestation-sig` *file*]
+
+# Description
+
+Unlike [`nix-store --restore`](./restore.md), this registers the path in the Nix database (so [`nix-copy-closure`](@docroot@/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md) can copy its closure). Unlike [`nix-store --import`](./import.md), the input is a raw NAR from `nix-store --dump`, not an export stream.
+
+The store path is the input-addressed path from the builder (it is **not** recomputed from the NAR hash).
+
+If `--attestation-json` / `--attestation-sig` are given, Nix verifies the cache signature (`trusted-public-keys`) and writes `{hashPart}.attestation.json` and `.sig` under `attestation-harmonia-dir` and `attestation-store`. Otherwise it looks for those files already in those directories (`bindAttestationSidecarFromDisk`).
+
+After this, `nix-copy-closure --to ssh://host store-path` sends each path's sidecar **before** the NAR (serve protocol 2.9). The remote `nix-store --serve --write` must be this Nix fork; stock Nix 2.8 skips the sidecar.
+
+`--references` should list runtime / direct-input store paths that are already valid (import leaves first).
+
+{{#include ./opt-common.md}}
+
+{{#include ../opt-common.md}}
+
+{{#include ../env-common.md}}
+
+# Examples
+
+```console
+$ nix-store --import-nar \
+    /nix/store/i0d0rjpig00qhhmf1qnvndavn82cfv22-jo-1.7 \
+    ./nars/sha256-….nar \
+    --nar-hash sha256-8F69FTswF4p69HBwztO27PUg8zMAm+r3VK0simezU5Q= \
+    --attestation-json ./certificates/harmonia/i0d0rjpig00qhhmf1qnvndavn82cfv22.attestation.json \
+    --attestation-sig  ./certificates/harmonia/i0d0rjpig00qhhmf1qnvndavn82cfv22.attestation.sig
+
+$ nix-copy-closure --to harmoniatest@host \
+    /nix/store/i0d0rjpig00qhhmf1qnvndavn82cfv22-jo-1.7
+```
